page DocsServerTerminal

title "Terminal - Documentation"

template
<div class="min-h-[calc(100vh-4rem)] grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] bg-page transition-colors">

  <DocsSidebar active="server-terminal" />

  <div class="min-w-0 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-10 py-6 sm:py-10">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

    <article class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel p-5 sm:p-8">
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Documentation / Inside a server</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-light uppercase tracking-wide text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Terminal</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-sm mt-2 mb-8">The Terminal page opens a shell on a server, right in your browser, with nothing to install. Open it with Terminal in the menu on the left.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-5">Opening a session</h2>

      <div class="space-y-7 mb-10">

        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-base font-semibold">Choose a server</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">Above the terminal is a row with one button per server, each with a coloured dot for its status. The one you came from is already selected. Switching to another server ends the current session. If you have no servers yet, the page offers Add a server.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-base font-semibold">Connect</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">The terminal says "Ready to connect" and tells you which user you will be. Select Connect. It shows "Opening a shell…" for a moment, then you have a prompt.</p>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-2">If a host key is pinned for the server, it is checked on every connection, including this one. See <a href="/docs/servers/settings" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">Server settings</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-base font-semibold">Confirm it is you</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">With two-factor sign-in on, a "Confirm it's you" box appears instead. Enter a code from your authenticator app, a recovery code, or the code from a text message, then select Verify and connect. If you have SMS set up, Text me a code sends one. Cancel goes back.</p>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-2">If the code is wrong, the box stays open with a message so you can try again.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Using the terminal</h2>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">The bar above the terminal shows user@host and a badge: Connecting, Connected, Verification needed or Disconnected. While you are connected, it also has these buttons:</p>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-4">

        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Copy</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Copies the text you selected in the terminal. It says "Copied" for a moment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Paste</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Types what is on your clipboard into the terminal.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Clear</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Wipes the screen. The session carries on.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Disconnect</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Ends the session.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Expand</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Makes the terminal larger, over the rest of the page. Choose Collapse, press Escape, or click outside it to go back.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">When a session ends for any reason, the badge turns to Disconnected and a Reconnect button appears.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">The idle limit</h2>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">A session closes after 15 minutes without typing. A thin bar along the top of the terminal shows how much of that time is left. At the bottom you see how long you have been connected, and the idle limit.</p>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">When two minutes are left, the bar turns amber and the note says "Closing in … without typing". Typing anything starts the 15 minutes again.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Quick checks</h2>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Below the terminal, a Quick checks card has one button for each common command. While you are connected, select one and it runs in your open session. Hover over a button to see the exact command. The same buttons appear along the bottom when the terminal is expanded.</p>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-3">

        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Disk</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5 font-mono">df -h</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Memory</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5 font-mono">free -h</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Top processes</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5 font-mono">top -bn1 | head -n 15</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Nginx status</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5 font-mono">systemctl status nginx --no-pager</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Nginx errors</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5 font-mono">sudo tail -n 50 /var/log/nginx/error.log</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Listening ports</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5 font-mono">sudo ss -tlnp</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">Before you connect, the card says to connect first. Commands that start with sudo need the SSH user to be root or have passwordless sudo.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">When your account is locked</h2>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">If your account is locked for payment, Connect and Reconnect are greyed out and say "Pay to continue", and the quick checks are off.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">If something goes wrong</h2>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden">

        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't open a terminal.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">A red box with Try again. The server did not answer. Check that it is online and that the host key has not changed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't load the terminal library.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The terminal is loaded from the internet when you first connect. Check your connection and try again.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Enter your verification code. / That code didn't work.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The code box was empty, or the code was wrong. Enter a fresh code. Too many wrong tries lock the prompt for a while.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Disconnected</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The session ended, often because of the idle limit. Select Reconnect to start a new one.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-8 pt-5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
        <a href="/docs/servers/logs" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">&larr; Logs</a>
        <a href="/docs/servers/settings" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">Settings &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
  </div>
</div>